# Content conventions

- Posts are `.mdx` files in `src/content/blog/`, slugs are lowercase-kebab-case (the filename becomes the URL: `/blog/<slug>/`).
- Frontmatter schema (enforced in `src/content.config.ts` via zod):
  - `title`: string (required)
  - `description`: string (recommended, used for SEO + list page)
  - `published`: ISO date (required)
  - `tags`: string[], kebab-case, default `[]`
  - `image`: string, optional
  - `draft`: boolean, default `false` — set `true` for work in progress
- Blog list filters drafts and sorts by `published` descending — do not work around this in pages.
- MDX is JSX-like: escape `{` and `<` in prose; code blocks must declare a language.
- Changes to the schema must be reflected in `AGENTS.md`, `docs/content-authoring.md`, and any affected pages.
